INPEX union members across the INPEX CPF, FPSO and ILNG facilities have once again delivered.
97.3% of the INPEX offshore and onshore operations workforce participated in the EA Ballot, with 97.5% of the 471 strong workforce voting ‘YES’ to an EBA which sets new industry standards for our members working direct for the Tier 1 oil & gas operators..
The INPEX EBA campaign had plenty going on. 
The non-union EA INPEX tried getting voted up in April this year got smashed up by 98% of the INPEX workforce.
INPEX’s S.424 application to the FWC to prevent members from exercising their legal rights to take Protected Industrial Action got smashed up the Union lawyers.
And INPEX’s decision to follow AREEA’s idiotic hard line IR agenda and push back against our members’ bargaining claims resulted in Extensive PIA across each of the INPEX facilities including:
• A tripped flashgas compressor on the FPSO with $600K per day going up in smoke;
• 2 Conde tankers and 1 LNG tanker not being loaded;
• 1 ILNG train being shutdown and
• $200 million of lost production.
The INPEX EBA campaign was a campaign where members stood shoulder to shoulder across each of the 3 INPEX facilities in fighting for & securing the following EBA outcomes:
1. Highest REM standards (salaries & allowances) amongst the 4 Tier-1 oil & gas Operators, with bonuses locked in & paid on a collective and not individual basis.
2. Maintenance contractor & labour hire minimum rates & conditions locked in;
3. Job security locked in for all INPEX facility and facility support members;
4. A new Career Progression Framework with level progression determined by agreed competencies and objective criteria;
5. Flights provided to all interstate members from Capital Cities and agreed regional airports;
6. 20 job share positions available to members on each of the 3 INPEX facilities;
7. Improved representational rights including union representation in meetings and investigations, Right of Entry provisions for OA Organisers on the offshore facilities, delegates rights, Consultative Committees & improved DSP provisions;
8. Overcycle for travel delays plus travel during mid-swing O/C with O/C being increased to X1.5 plus superannuation (equivalent of X 1.7);
9. Additional 14 paid days Supplementary Leave, improved Personal Leave, option to take double LSL on half pay and improved Parental Leave;
10. Improved redundancy provisions plus agreed redundancy criteria (voluntary first then last-on first-off next);
11. Agreed processes for changes in panels, shifts & facilities & hours of work provisions tightened up;
12. Income Protection exclusions removed with job security for employees in receipt of income protection;
13. Facility standards locked in including catering, recreational areas and unlimited unmetered Wi-Fi capable of supporting un-interrupted video conferencing;
14. Improved fatigue management including minimum rest periods (and unoccupied cabins) for Night Shift employees mobilising to the facilities, minimum breaks between shifts and call-outs;
Great work by our Workplace Reps who put in a massive effort during bargaining, and our broader offshore West Coast membership (together with the AWU & ETU members at ILNG) who backed in their mates and the Union and never took a backward step at any stage throughout our bargaining campaign.
The AREEA peanut gallery stands condemned for their public attack and campaign against one of the world’s highest skilled and competent oil and gas workforces. 
The irony isn’t lost on us that AREEA’s attack on INPEX workers came from an outfit full of HR bosses and wannabe’s who would be lucky to know how to change a light bulb, let alone work on a LNG facility.
AREEA should not under-estimate the role their public condemnation of our INPEX members had in stiffening the resolve of our INPEX members to go One Day Longer & One Day Stronger in their Fight for a Union Standard EBA.
IF YOU DON’T FIGHT, YOU LOSE!
